{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>By the rivers of Babylon</b> — At the beginning of the book I mentioned the view of the commentators on this psalm, and this psalm is spoken in the voice of the Levites, for they are the singers, in their exile in Babylon." "<b>By the rivers</b> means: in their seclusion away from the Babylonians, so that they would not hear their weeping. Moreover: because they said, \"There we hung up our lyres.\"" "<b>We sat</b> means: as ones stunned. [It is like] יושב משמים; therefore the word גם."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 137, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra apparently reads יושב משמים as a phrase illustrating stunned sitting; possibly a truncated or obscure exemplum, rendered here hyper-literally without expanding."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:57.677729312Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}